00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.920
- [Instructor] We are told
that 52 times 762 is equal

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.920
to 39,624, and then we're
told to match each expression

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.410
to its product.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.290
And these products, this is an exercise

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.270
on Khan Academy, you can move them around

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.000
so the product can be matched
to the appropriate expression.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.230
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.800
All right, now what you
might have realized is all

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.490
of these expressions
deal with the same digits

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.870
as 52 times 762.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.400
They just have the decimal
in different places.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.540
And so what we can do
is, we can say, hey look,

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.210
the answer is going to have
the digits three, nine,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.780
six, two, four, in that order.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.480
And you could see all of
these have the digits three,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.250
nine, six, two, four, in that order.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.800
And then we can estimate what

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.570
these expressions should be equal to,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.260
what the products should be equal to,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.810
to think about the decimal.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:57.810
So this first expression, 0.52 times 76.2,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.010
the way I think about
it is 0.52, that's close

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.550
to 50/100, that's close to a half,

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.690
and so 76.2, that's close to 76.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.850
And so this first expression,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.410
this first product should
be roughly half of 76.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.000
Half of 76 would be around 38.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.520
And so which of these is close to 38?

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.000
Well this first one is 39.624,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.630
so that's actually the closest to 38.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.750
The second one is 396.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.500
And then we have 3,962.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.731
So I like this first one, the 39.624.

00:01:33.731 --> 00:01:35.840
That feels right.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.047
Now the second expression,

00:01:37.047 --> 00:01:40.970
0.52 times 762.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.810
Well once again, 0.52 is
roughly equal to 50/100,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.930
roughly equal to 5/10,
roughly equal to 1/2,

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.210
and so, and 762, we
could say hey, you know,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.010
that's, if we wanna be really rough,

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.100
really, really approximate it,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.200
we could say, hey, it's roughly 800.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.690
And so this should be about half of 800,

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.120
so it should be around 400.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.690
And so we actually had
that choice already there.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.960
So this would be 396.24.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:12.030
Definitely wouldn't be the the 3,962.4.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.860
And so I'm already feeling good

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.290
that this last choice sits down here.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.234
But I can verify it.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:21.100
5.2, well let's just say that's roughly 5.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.200
762, let's say that's roughly 800.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.970
So five times 800, that would be around,

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.450
that would be 4000.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.110
And so we would expect this expression

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.200
to be close to 4000, and indeed,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.510
that's what this choice is.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.060
So it turns out that it
was already in the order

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.220
that we needed it to be, but it's good

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.420
that we checked on that.

